  "explanation": {
    "markdown": "## Past simple negatives and questions\n\nWe use **did** and **didn’t** to make negatives, questions and short answers in past simple.  \n  \n![Grammar chart outlining the structure of the past simple tense in positive, negative, and question forms, with examples and common mistakes.](/uploads/grammar/a1/past-simple-negatives-questions/img-1.jpg)\n\n#### Word order in questions\n\nRemember that the [word order in questions](https://test-english.com/grammar-points/a1/questions/) is **QWASI**: (Question Word), Auxiliary (did), Subject, Infinitive.  \n  \n![Grammar chart demonstrating how to form questions in the past simple tense using 'was/were' with 'be' and 'did' with other verbs.](/uploads/grammar/a1/past-simple-negatives-questions/img-2.jpg)\n\n#### Infinitive without **to**\n\nWe use **did** or **didn’t** with the **bare infinitive** of the main verb (= infinitive without **to**).\n\n-   *I **didn’t** **work** yesterday.* ![](/uploads/grammar/a1/past-simple-negatives-questions/img-3.png)\n-   *I didn’t **didn’t worked** yesterday. ![](/uploads/grammar/a1/past-simple-negatives-questions/img-4.png)* \n-   ***Did** you **go** to the concert?* ![](/uploads/grammar/a1/past-simple-negatives-questions/img-5.png)\n-   ***Did** you **went** to the concert? ![](/uploads/grammar/a1/past-simple-negatives-questions/img-6.png)* \n\n#### Don’t use **did** in positive sentences\n\nWe use **did** or **didn’t** in negatives, questions and short answers, but **NOT in positive sentences**.\n\n-   *We **stayed** home yesterday.* ![](/uploads/grammar/a1/past-simple-negatives-questions/img-7.png)\n-   *We **did stay** home yesterday. ![](/uploads/grammar/a1/past-simple-negatives-questions/img-8.png)* \n-   *I **went** out last night.* ![](/uploads/grammar/a1/past-simple-negatives-questions/img-9.png)\n-   *I **did go** out last night. ![](/uploads/grammar/a1/past-simple-negatives-questions/img-10.png)* \n\n#### **Did** or **was/were**?\n\nWe use **did** and **didn’t** (NOT [**was/wasn’t** or **were/weren’t**](https://test-english.com/grammar-points/a1/was-were/)) as the auxiliary verb in negatives and questions in past simple.\n\n-   *We **didn’t eat** at 6.* ![](/uploads/grammar/a1/past-simple-negatives-questions/img-11.png)\n-   *We **weren’t eat** at 6. ![](/uploads/grammar/a1/past-simple-negatives-questions/img-12.png)* \n-   ***Did** you **do** your homework?* ![](/uploads/grammar/a1/past-simple-negatives-questions/img-13.png)\n-   ***Were** you **do** your homework? ![](/uploads/grammar/a1/past-simple-negatives-questions/img-14.png)* \n\nWe do **NOT** use **did** or **didn’t** in past simple negatives or questions when the **main verb** is **be**.\n\n-   *They **weren’t** happy.* ![](/uploads/grammar/a1/past-simple-negatives-questions/img-15.png)\n-   *They **didn’t be** happy. ![](/uploads/grammar/a1/past-simple-negatives-questions/img-16.png)* \n-   ***Was** he at home?* ![](/uploads/grammar/a1/past-simple-negatives-questions/img-17.png)\n-   ***Did** he **be** at home? ![](/uploads/grammar/a1/past-simple-negatives-questions/img-18.png)*",
